 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
+## Freezing
+
+`POST /projects/{pid}/freeze` freezes a project. Only a manager of the project may
+freeze it (other members → 403, non-members → 404, archived → 409).
+
+- Every member of the project, managers included, is changed to `viewer`.
+- The response is the member list after the change, ordered by user ID:
+  `[{"userId":"ann","role":"viewer"}, ...]`.
+- The project is marked frozen. Task writes (create, update, delete) are then
+  refused with 409 `project is frozen`. In practice they are already refused with
+  403, because nobody in a frozen project is a contributor or manager any more.
+- Reads still work. Other projects are not affected.
+- Assignments are kept. A task may still be assigned to a user who is now a viewer,
+  because the assignee rule does not apply to frozen projects.
+- Freezing cannot be undone through the API, and a second freeze is refused, since
+  no one is a manager after the first one.
+
 ## Seed data
 
